Error: Jet.ReturnTypeMismatch: This value is `vis2.bank.Account`, but `bad` returns bank.Account
  --> Tests/UI/inline_module_return_type_mismatch.jet:15:36
    |
 15 | bad: fn() -> bank.Account { return vis2.bank.Account{balance: 1} }
    |                                    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: `bad` declares bank.Account as its result, so the value it hands back must be bank.Account
 Fix: Hand back a bank.Account value: convert this value to bank.Account, or return the value you meant
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.ReturnTypeMismatch
